        "text": "This ceramic project depicts a hybrid head—half dead coral, half human face. The coral side is cracked and hollow, while the human side is realistic and expressive, full of life. This contrast serves as a visual metaphor for the environmental crisis we face. As coral reefs die, it's not just nature that suffers—it’s a reflection of our own vulnerability. Through this work, I hope to raise awareness about the urgency of protecting our oceans and the ecosystems that sustain us.",
